  "response": "```python\ndef topological_order(tasks, dependencies):\n▁▁▁▁\"\"\"\n▁▁▁▁Returns the lexicographically smallest valid topological ordering of tasks,\n▁▁▁▁or [] if a cycle is detected or if some tasks are not present in the input.\n\n▁▁▁▁Args:\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁tasks (list): A list of task names (strings).\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁dependencies (list): A list of tuples, where each tuple represents a dependency\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁(task1, task2), meaning task1 must be completed before task2.\n\n▁▁▁▁Returns:\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁list: A list representing the topological order of tasks, or an empty list if a cycle exists.\n▁▁▁▁\"\"\"\n\n▁▁▁▁in_degree = {task: 0 for task in tasks}\n▁▁▁▁graph = {task: [] for task in tasks}\n\n▁▁▁▁for dependency in dependencies:\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁task1, task2 = dependency\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁if task1 not in tasks or task2 not in tasks:\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁return []▁▁# Invalid input: missing tasks\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁graph[task1].append(task2)\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁in_degree[task2] += 1\n\n▁▁▁▁queue = [task for task in tasks if in_degree[task] == 0]\n▁▁▁▁result = []\n\n▁▁▁▁while queue:\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁task = min(queue)▁▁# Lexicographically smallest\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁queue.remove(task)\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁result.append(task)\n\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁for neighbor in graph[task]:\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁in_degree[neighbor] -= 1\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁if in_degree[neighbor] == 0:\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁queue.append(neighbor)\n\n▁▁▁▁if len(result) != len(tasks):\n▁▁▁▁▁▁▁▁return []▁▁# Cycle detected\n\n▁▁▁▁return result\n```",
